/*
# Seed Initial Data: Categories and Products

## Overview
Populates the database with the 9 existing categories and 26 products
that were previously hardcoded in the frontend. This ensures the store
has identical content when switching to database-driven data.

## Data
- 9 categories (tshirts, shirts, hoodies, jeans, dresses, sneakers, bags, watches, accessories)
- 26 products with bilingual names/descriptions, prices, images, colors, sizes, tags

## Notes
- Uses ON CONFLICT to be idempotent (safe to re-run)
- Product IDs match the original hardcoded IDs for cart/wishlist localStorage compatibility
- Colors stored as jsonb array of {name, hex} objects
*/

-- ============================================================
-- CATEGORIES
-- ============================================================
ON CONFLICT (key) DO NOTHING;

-- ============================================================
-- PRODUCTS (26 items)
-- ============================================================
ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

-- Sync the serial sequence so new products get the next available id
SELECT setval('products_id_seq', (SELECT MAX(id) FROM products));